Thought: Adding skip to 2<-1 slightly hurt (0.4237 vs 0.4272). The best config so far is: 1<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-1: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-1: skip_connect, 3<-2: nor_conv_3x3 with perf=0.4272.

Let me try a few more variations. Maybe try nor_conv_1x1 on 3<-1 instead of skip, or try avg_pool on some edge. Let me also try 1<-0 as skip_connect since the first edge often benefits from identity. Let me try 1<-0 as skip.

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "skip_connect", "2<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-1": "skip_connect", "3<-2": "nor_conv_3x3"}

Thought: The 1x1 conv on 2<-1 dropped performance to 0.424667. So nor_conv_3x3 on 2<-1 is better. Let me try a few more variations. Let me try changing 1<-0 to nor_conv_3x3 while keeping the rest of the best config.

Best so far: {"1<-0": "skip_connect", "2<-0": "skip_connect", "2<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-1": "skip_connect", "3<-2": "nor_conv_3x3"} = 0.441056

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "skip_connect", "2<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-1": "skip_connect", "3<-2": "nor_conv_3x3"}

Thought: All nor_conv_3x3 gives 0.411111. That's a big jump. Let me try variations. The known best in NAS-Bench-201 (on CIFAR-10) is often the architecture with: 1<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-1: nor_conv_1x1, 3<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-1: skip_connect, 3<-2: nor_conv_1x1 — roughly. Let me test a config that mixes conv_3x3 on the "input" edges and conv_1x1/skip on later ones. Let me try replacing some 3x3 with 1x1 to reduce params and possibly improve.

Try: 1<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-0: nor_conv_1x1, 2<-1: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-1: nor_conv_1x1, 3<-2: nor_conv_3x3.

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "nor_conv_1x1", "2<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-1": "nor_conv_1x1", "3<-2": "nor_conv_3x3"}

Thought: Mixing conv_1x1 improved performance to 0.428278. Let me continue exploring. I'll try a known strong NAS-Bench-201 architecture. The best architecture found in NAS-Bench-201 for CIFAR-10 is often reported as: |nor_conv_3x3~0| + |nor_conv_3x3~0|nor_conv_3x3~1| + |skip_connect~0|nor_conv_3x3~1|nor_conv_3x3~2|. Or similar. Let me try introducing skip_connect on some edges.

Try: 1<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-1: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-0: skip_connect, 3<-1: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-2: nor_conv_3x3.

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-0": "skip_connect", "3<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-2": "nor_conv_3x3"}

Thought: Adding skip_connect on 3<-0 improved to 0.463556. Let me try more skip connections and variations. Let me test the known best NAS-Bench-201 architecture: |nor_conv_3x3~0| + |nor_conv_3x3~0|nor_conv_3x3~1| + |skip_connect~0|nor_conv_3x3~1|nor_conv_3x3~2| — that's what I just tried essentially. Let me try variations with skip_connect on other edges.

Try: 1<-0: nor_conv_3x3, 2<-0: skip_connect, 2<-1: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-0: skip_connect, 3<-1: nor_conv_3x3, 3<-2: nor_conv_3x3.

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "skip_connect", "2<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-0": "skip_connect", "3<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-2": "nor_conv_3x3"}

Thought: This configuration gave 0.398278, which is worse than the best so far (0.432667). Let me try a variation that's closer to the best one, perhaps adding a 1x1 convolution or trying different placements of skip connections. The best config was {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-1": "skip_connect", "3<-0": "skip_connect", "3<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-2": "skip_connect"}.

Let me try replacing one operation with nor_conv_1x1 to see if it helps, or try a slightly different arrangement.

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-1": "skip_connect", "3<-0": "skip_connect", "3<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-2": "nor_conv_1x1"}
